Nowadays, some people think competition at work, school, and in daily life makes people work harder, while others believe cooperation is more important for society. Some people say competition helps people improve, but others disagree. In my opinion, both views have some truth, but cooperation is more useful for society.

Those who support competition argue that it pushes people to improve themself. For example, students study harder when they compete for grades, and this shows that competition can create motivation.

On the other hand, others believe cooperation helps people achieve more together. Although working alone sometimes has benefits.

Admittedly, opponents may contend that competition also makes the workplace more efficient, because employees work hard to get promotions. However, they overlook that too much competition often causes stress and conflict between colleagues.

In conclusion, I believe cooperation is more beneficial than competition in most situations, because it creates a better environment for everyone in society and helps people work together happily.